WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.065
Idea. Before a football season, a team sets a target: win the league, or just avoid relegation. A business does the same. Its targets are called objectives.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:18.847
Objectives give the owner and staff a clear direction, motivate them, and give a target to check progress against.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:26.828
Financial objectives are about money: survival, profit, sales, market share, and financial security.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:42.940
Non-financial objectives are not mainly about money: social objectives, personal satisfaction, challenge, independence and control. A social objective aims to help society or the environment, such as cutting waste.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:53.542
Objectives also change as a business evolves: because of market conditions, new technology, its own results, new laws, or growth and new owners.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:04.513
Method. Step one: decide whether the objective is financial or non-financial. Watch out: survival and market share are both financial.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:11.477
Step two: find what the owner or business in the case actually wants, using a detail from the case.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:19.699
Step three: in an explain answer, give one point, then ask so what, twice. That gives one point and two linked steps.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:34.376
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper two in November 2025, about Samsung. Explain one advantage to a business of having a social objective. It is worth three marks.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:40.890
Mark one is the advantage. A social objective can improve the business's reputation.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:48.991
Mark two explains why. When Samsung is seen to help society, customers are more likely to trust and like the brand.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:58.369
Mark three gives the consequence. More people may choose its phones and televisions instead of rivals such as Apple, so its sales rise.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:07.754
Common mistake. Mistake one: calling survival or market share non-financial. Both are financial objectives.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:17.831
Mistake two: defining social objective when the question asks for an advantage. A definition is not an advantage, so it earns no marks here.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:35.590
Your turn. Now you try. Maya opens a small bakery. She wants to stay open through her first year, and she gives leftover bread to a local shelter every evening. Which objective is financial, and which is non-financial? Pause and decide.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:48.790
Answer. Staying open through her first year is survival, a financial objective. Giving bread to the shelter helps the community, so it is a social objective, which is non-financial.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:59.567
Remember the method: sort the objective, fit it to the business in the case, then build one point with two linked steps. Now try the practice questions for this type.
